messages.text:
Colleague: begin tensor linearization directly from the ensemble co-metric, not from a generic metric perturbation inserted by hand.

Take the isotropic background

[
\bar C_\perp^{ij}=\sigma^2\bar h^{ij},
\qquad
h_{ij}=(C_\perp^{-1})_{ij},
]

and perturb its transverse-traceless sector:

[
C_\perp^{ij}

\bar C_\perp^{ij}
+
\delta C_{\rm TT}^{ij},
\qquad
\nabla_i\delta C_{\rm TT}^{ij}=0,
\qquad
\bar h_{ij}\delta C_{\rm TT}^{ij}=0.
]

Then

[
q_{ij}\equiv\delta h_{ij}^{\rm TT}

-\bar h_{ik},\delta C_{\rm TT}^{kl},\bar h_{lj}.
]

The quadratic tensor action must have the isotropic form

[
S_T^{(2)}

\frac18\int d\tau,d^3x,a^3
\left[
A_T\dot q_{ij}\dot q^{ij}

\frac{B_T}{a^2}\nabla_kq_{ij}\nabla^kq^{ij}

\frac{D_T}{a^4}(\Delta q_{ij})^2

M_T^2q_{ij}q^{ij}
\right].
]

Its principal relation is

[
A_T\omega^2

B_T\frac{k^2}{a^2}
+
D_T\frac{k^4}{a^4}.
]

Audit conditions:

[
A_T>0
]

for no kinetic ghost,

[
B_T>0
]

for gradient stability,

[
c_{\rm tensor}^2=\frac{B_T}{A_T}=c^2
]

for the low-frequency light cone, and identical coefficients for both helicities for no birefringence.

The present bending coefficient (\kappa) naturally contributes to (D_T), the (k^4) term. It does not by itself generate (B_T). A genuine network-tension or first-gradient term must emerge from coarse-graining the filament ensemble.

Important correction: BV ghosts are gauge-bookkeeping fields, not simply discarded transverse filament orientations. The BV push-forward may renormalize (A_T,B_T,D_T), but only after the microscopic action and measure are defined.

The diameter hypothesis does not repair the aperture gap. Replacing radius by diameter doubles (a/p), moving the complementary angle from about (32.9^\circ) to roughly (17.9^\circ), farther from (36.5^\circ).

So the next calculation is the Hessian of the coarse-grained filament energy with respect to (\delta C_{\rm TT}^{ij}).
